    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθ-ήνιος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθ-άνιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνία</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>obedient to the rein</i>, of a horse, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				30
			</span></i> : metaph., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.592c
			</span></i>: generally, <i>obedient</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					1.17
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				101
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.90b
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στράτευμα</span>
			<i>well-disciplined</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				10.9
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					16p.456M.
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π</span>. <i>submissiveness,
				docility</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.442c
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				102e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.184
			</span></i>; in Surgery, <i>gently</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
			</span></i>
			
				Med.
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.18.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.70b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>that makes obedient</i>, 
